Surfaced by k21. ADR 0011 (accepted) is only half-built: Lib::keys() sorts nothing for a plain Perl hashref caller context -- its own inline comment says the rest of ADR 0011, sorting plain caller hashes, is still open. Result: a plain hashref context value iterates in raw, per-process-random Perl hash order (observed as real flakiness across PERL_HASH_SEED values). ADR 0011 decided plain caller hashes are SORTED. Fix: sort keys in the plain-hashref branch of Lib::keys (the Hash::Ordered branch is already correct). dump/dictsort/list/items over plain hashes may share this or stay with k17.

2026-09-22 21:15 Sort landed in Lib::keys (lib/Text/Nunjucks/Lib.pm:338). ADR 0011 fully built:
plain caller hashes now go through `sort CORE::keys` so a {b:1,a:2,c:3}
context hash iterates a,b,c deterministically across PERL_HASH_SEED values
(perl-level hash order is the documented divergence from JS insertion order).
Hash::Ordered keeps its own (insertion) order, matching JS Object.keys.

